      "log_sha256": "3760ddaefb2e19d1a279d810819c2eac632dcdb3712fe57eddfe8d866f23f2b1",
      "character_offset": 129040,
      "tool_use_id": "call_00_n4qGwhFLaj5lnbN05vrx0608",
      "arguments": {
        "description": "Profile hardswish round 1",
        "subagent_type": "kernel-profile-analyzer",
        "prompt": "Profile KernelGen round_num=1 for the operator `hardswish` in this workspace (tmp/main.py, seed: streaming hardswish Triton kernel with cached compiled launch; grid capped at 40 programs for n>=131072, BLOCK<=4096, loop over N with N as tl.constexpr).\n\nUse `mcp__kernelgen__get_profile_context` with `hgkda_workloads` to obtain the exact native inputs for the frozen workloads, and profile representative timing workloads so we can separate host-launch cost from device cost and understand the 4096x4096 cases.\n\nAuthoritative round-1 measurements (do not recompute or contradict them):\n- geo_mean 0.6537, 30/30 PASSED.\n- hardswish-timing-0 (f16, 1024): cand 0.02667 ms vs ref 0.01930 ms (0.724x)\n- hardswish-timing-2 (f16, 1048576): cand 0.02757 vs ref 0.01898 (0.688x)\n- hardswish-timing-3 (f16, 4096x4096): cand 0.09738 vs ref 0.04206 (0.432x)\n- hardswish-timing-7 (bf16, 4096x4096): cand 0.09952 vs ref 0.04426 (0.445x)\n- hardswish-timing-11 (f32, 4096x4096): cand 0.11573 vs ref 0.09263 (0.800x)\n\nQuestions the profile should answer:\n1. Device kernel time for a tiny workload (e.g. timing-0, 1024 elements) versus the ~26.7 us full-call time: how much is host launch overhead? What is the standalone device task duration?\n2. For timing-3 (f16 4096x4096) and timing-11 (f32 4096x4096): actual device kernel duration, per-block MTE2/MTE3/Vector active ratios, and any evidence the 40-program grid with a 1024-iteration serial loop under-utilizes the machine (e.g. low MTE2 activity, high Scalar/wait, low bandwidth). Compare with the reference-side or an equivalent high-parallelism organization if the tooling allows.\n3. Whether the device time is consistent with logical-byte/elapsed throughput estimates, and how far it is from a plausible bandwidth ceiling (do NOT call logical throughput measured HBM bandwidth).\n\nReturn one concrete, actionable next experiment. Keep the analysis bounded; record it with mcp__kernelgen__record_profile_analysis. Do not edit tmp/main.py."
      }
    }
  ],
  "note": "原始分析和 manifest 字节保持不变；附件使用短路径平铺，旧绝对路径可通过 source_path 映射到 archived_path。"
}
